meta {
  name: Create Channel
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/clients/{{clientId}}/channels
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "type": "email",
    "name": "Sales team",
    "description": "Inbound leads",
    "emailAddresses": ["sales@acme.com"]
  }
}

docs {
  Creates a channel with its type-specific half in one transaction (SOL-49).
  The body is keyed on type:
    email: { type, name, description?, emailAddresses: [at least one] }
    slack: { type, name, description?, webhookUrl: "https://hooks.slack.com/..." }
  Fields from the other type are rejected (422).

  201 responds with the same shape as Get Channel. 404 if the client doesn't
  exist; 409 CONFLICT if the client already has a channel with this name.
}
